<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry VII of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1457">1457</a>–<a href="/years/1509">1509</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Henry Tudor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry VII, born Henry Tudor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pembroke-castle">Pembroke Castle</a> in 1457, was the Lancastrian claimant who defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-iii-of-england">Richard III</a> at Bosworth in 1485 and became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-tudor">Tudor dynasty</a>. His marriage to Elizabeth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> joined the rival houses of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>. He restored royal finances, curbed the great nobles and was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england.jpg" alt="Henry VII of England" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enrique_VII_de_Inglaterra,_por_un_artista_an%C3%B3nimo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
